==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
{{confix|poly|omino}} ([[poly-]] + [[domino|(d)omino]]), as if the ''d'' were for [[di-]], two, a domino being made up of two squares

===Noun===
{{en-noun|polyominoes}}

# {{context|geometry|lang=en}} A [[polyform]] made by joining one or more [[square]]s edge to edge in various [[arrangement]]s.

====Synonyms====
*[[n-omino|''n''-omino]]

====Related terms====
* [[-omino]]
* [[monomino]] (1 square)
* [[domino]] (2 squares)
* [[triomino]], [[tromino]] (3 squares)
* [[tetromino]] (4 squares)
* [[pentomino]] (5 squares) 
* [[hexomino]] (6 squares)
* [[heptomino]] (7 squares)
* [[octomino]] (8 squares)
* [[nonomino]] (9 squares)
* [[decomino]] (10 squares)

